{
 "about": "Field classes of the manipulation domain (VERIFY_HARDENING 6.3, lint L-WATCH; WP-D manipulation). 'fields' classifies, for this domain's types (house_sim/data/types/manipulation.json), every property of the type data the kernel's name table (watch_fields.json) does not, a few the kernel table misfits for these types (text: a price tag's printed price, identity; heat_limit_c / max_temp_c: a trivet's and a sheet's rated limits, identity, not process) and every field this domain's verbs and systems write: identity = what a thing is (static props); placement = where and how it sits (stack, pack, insert, cover, clip and lean records); setting = a configuration the robot sets (zipper, velcro, knots, closures, caps and threads, covers, tape, inflation, assembly); condition = damage in its worse direction (true is worse unless 'worse' says false or up); content = what it holds (cards, pieces, a game's components; rain pooled on a cover is a mess load the mess balance judges, guard mess); process = transient physics (falling, rolling, mixing); bookkeeping = records of what happened and mirrors of other things' placements (receptacles' items, a stack base's count, attached part lists: the things themselves are judged). 'types': per-type entries (a consumable roll's length_m is content: tearing wrap or tape off uses it up, allowed by envelope.consume). 'water_sensitive': paper, cardboard and framed prints (house.wet). 'writes': the field names of 'fields' this domain writes on things of ANY type (core mugs, plates, bags, other domains' covers and cords); the ledger applies a domain's 'fields' only to its own types, so for other types these names fall back to the kernel table or the default (setting: watched, a false alarm at worst, never a hole) until the kernel reads this list (request to WP1).",
